Aim

To configure Oracle Cloud storage services for storing application files, backups, and user data securely.

Requirements
Oracle Cloud Account
Internet Connection
Sample files for upload
Step 1: Login to Oracle Cloud

Open:

Oracle Cloud Console

Enter:

Username
Password

Click:

Sign In

Step 2: Open Storage Service

Click:

☰ Menu (Top Left)

Go to:

Storage
→ Buckets

If not visible:
Search:

Buckets

Step 3: Select Compartment

On left side:

Select your compartment.

Example:

MyLabCompartment
Step 4: Create Bucket

Click:

Create Bucket

Step 5: Enter Bucket Details

Fill:

Field	Value
Bucket Name	my-storage-bucket
Default Storage Tier	Standard
Encryption	Oracle Managed Key

Keep other settings default.

Click:

Create

Bucket is created successfully.

Step 6: Open Bucket

Click:

my-storage-bucket

Now bucket dashboard opens.

Step 7: Upload Files

Click:

Upload

Choose:

PDF
Image
Text file
Backup file

Click:

Upload Files

Wait until upload completes.

Step 8: Verify Uploaded Files

Inside bucket you can see:

File name
Size
Upload time

This confirms upload success.

Step 9: Download File Test

Click:

Three Dots (⋮)

Select:

Download

Verify file downloads properly.

Step 10: Configure Bucket Visibility

Go to:

Edit Visibility

Select:

Private Bucket

Click:

Save Changes

This keeps files secure.

Step 11: Configure User Access

Go to:

Identity & Security
→ Policies

Click:

Create Policy

Enter:

Field	Value
Name	StoragePolicy

Policy statement:

Allow group Developers to manage object-family in compartment MyLabCompartment

Click:

Create

Now authorized users can access storage.

Step 12: Monitor Storage Usage

Go to:

Bucket Details

Check:

Storage used
Number of objects
Bucket size
Step 13: Delete File (Optional)

Select uploaded file.

Click:

Delete

This demonstrates storage management.

Implementation & Result

Successfully:

Created storage bucket
Uploaded files
Downloaded files
Configured bucket security
Applied access policies

Cloud storage service was configured successfully.
